<section>
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>Turn measured losses into actions</h2>
      <p>Start with the observed signal, verify its cause, then change the part of the system that created the loss.</p>
      <table borders="rows" striped="false" col-widths="[23,35,42]">
        <tr>
          <th background-color="surface">Measured signal</th>
          <th background-color="surface">Verify the cause</th>
          <th background-color="surface">Action</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td valign="middle"><span text-color="accent"><b>Low field efficiency</b></span></td>
          <td valign="middle">Time turns and refills.</td>
          <td valign="middle">Redesign routes and stage inputs before work begins.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td valign="middle"><span text-color="accent"><b>Low capacity</b></span></td>
          <td valign="middle">Check actual speed, working width and available power.</td>
          <td valign="middle">Correct the limiting mismatch; do not raise speed if quality or soil conditions deteriorate.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td valign="middle"><span text-color="accent"><b>High cost/ha</b></span></td>
          <td valign="middle">Inspect idle time, fuel, repairs and annual utilization.</td>
          <td valign="middle">Reduce avoidable idle hours and match ownership or hire cost to expected use.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td valign="middle"><span text-color="accent"><b>Poor work quality</b></span></td>
          <td valign="middle">Measure overlap, misses and depth.</td>
          <td valign="middle">Calibrate before increasing speed or capacity.</td>
        </tr>
      </table>
      <grid spacing="none" vertical-sizing="hug">
        <grid-item background-color="accent" padding="12pt 16pt">
          <p><b>Track together:</b> ha/hour, field efficiency, cost/ha, fuel/ha, downtime and work quality.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>